# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the Python-driven leg of the sanitizer
# lane (.github/workflows/sanitizers.yml, pytest-tsan job).
#
# The interpreter process preloads the shared TSan runtime so the
# ctypes-loaded kith libraries resolve their instrumentation against one
# runtime instance. Every framework-side access is instrumented, so
# framework races report normally and findings stay attributable to
# framework code.
#
# The entry covers one class the lane cannot triage: libpq is
# uninstrumented third-party code, so a race whose stack carries a libpq
# frame has at most one instrumented side (an interceptor such as write)
# and no both-side visibility. The db module's own state is instrumented,
# so a defect confined to kith code reports independently with framework
# frames only. A mixed pair — a kith-db call racing a libpq-internal
# access — is suppressed here; the sanitizer lane's tsan ctest leg links
# the same libpq with no suppression file and is the independent detector
# for that shape.
called_from_lib:libpq
